.TH EMACS-REMOTE-CLIENT 1 "2026-11-21" "GNU Emacs" "GNU"
.\" NAME should be all caps, SECTION should be 1-8, maybe w/ subsection
.\" other params are allowed: see man(7), man(1)
.SH NAME
emacs\-remote\-client \- show the frames of a remote display session of Emacs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B emacs\-remote\-client
.I "[options] socket"
.br
.B emacs\-remote\-client
.I "[options]"
.B \-\-ssh
.I host
.br
.B emacs\-remote\-client \-\-relay
.I "[\-\-listen=spec] socket"
.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page documents briefly the
.B emacs\-remote\-client
command.
.PP
An Emacs that is configured with
.B \-\-with\-remote\-display
shows its frames on a remote display session.  Each session has a
Unix-domain socket.
.B emacs\-remote\-client
connects to a session and shows each frame of the session in a window
on the local display.  The keyboard and the mouse input of the windows
goes to Emacs.
.PP
The program has these modes:
.TP
.B SOCKET
Connect to the Unix-domain socket SOCKET of a session, and show its
frames.  When the connection ends, or no bytes come from the server
for the timeout, the program keeps its windows and connects to the
socket again.
.TP
.B \-\-ssh HOST
Start a new session on HOST through
.BR ssh (1),
or resume an open session with
.BR \-\-session .
The Emacs server on HOST must run.  The program runs
.B emacsclient
and
.B "emacs\-remote\-client \-\-relay"
on HOST through SSH, and then connects to the relay with TLS.
.TP
.B \-\-relay
Be the relay on the host of the session.  The relay connects the
session socket and the client.  It must be the first argument.
.TP
.B \-\-render\-to=FILE.png
Open no window.  When the server closes the connection, write the
first frame to FILE.png, and stop.  This mode needs no display.
.SH OPTIONS
The options start with two dashes ("\-\-"), as the long options of
the GNU command line syntax.
.TP
.B \-H, \-\-help
Print the usage information message and exit.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version of Emacs and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-timeout=MS
Connect again after MS milliseconds with no bytes from the server.
The default is 15000, and the minimum is 3.  A slow network can need
a larger value.
.TP
.B \-\-render\-to=FILE.png
Open no window.  When the server closes the connection, write the
first frame to FILE.png, and stop.
.TP
.B \-\-ssh HOST
Start a new session on HOST through SSH, and connect to it through a
relay on HOST.
.TP
.B \-\-ssh\-command=PROGRAM
With \-\-ssh, run PROGRAM as SSH.  The default is "ssh".
.TP
.B \-\-listen=SPEC
Let the relay listen at SPEC: ADDRESS, ADDRESS:PORT, or
ADDRESS:LOW\-HIGH, with an IPv6 ADDRESS in brackets.  The relay
listens on the first free port of the range.  The default is the
server address of SSH, and the ports 60001\-61000.
.TP
.B \-\-connect=ADDRESS
With \-\-ssh, connect to the relay at ADDRESS.  The default is the
host name that "ssh \-G HOST" gives.
.TP
.B \-\-session=NAME
With \-\-ssh, resume the open session NAME, and do not start a new
session.  NAME has 1 to 32 letters, digits, and "\-" characters.
.TP
.B \-\-relay
Be the relay for the session socket SOCKET.  It must be the first
argument.  The client runs "emacs\-remote\-client \-\-relay" on HOST
through SSH.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
The exit status is 0 on success, and 1 on an error.  When the user ends
the session, for example with C-x C-c, the exit status is 0.  When the
session does not exist, for example because Emacs stopped, the exit
status is 1.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SSH_CONNECTION
With
.B \-\-relay
and no
.BR \-\-listen ,
the relay listens at the server address in this variable, which
.BR sshd (8)
sets.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
The directory of the cache of the fonts.  The default is "~/.cache".
.TP
.B DISPLAY, WAYLAND_DISPLAY
The display of the windows.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/remote\-client/
The fonts that the server sent, and the hashes of the local fonts.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start a new session on the host "workstation", and show its frames:
.PP
.RS
emacs\-remote\-client \-\-ssh workstation
.RE
.PP
Resume the open session "remote\-2" on that host:
.PP
.RS
emacs\-remote\-client \-\-ssh workstation \-\-session=remote\-2
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR emacs (1),
.BR emacsclient (1),
.BR ssh (1)
.SH COPYING
